From 7c9d9d6be1ffb794c47336d6e87f71b8dac038f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:04:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mailbox: mtk-gpueb: Clear the RX state before passing the
 message on

The threaded handler marked the channel empty only after the client's
rx_callback had returned. A client that sends its next message as soon
as it is woken by the callback, as mtk-mfg-pmdomain does when it sets the
OPP right after powering the GPU on, can reach send_data() while the
channel still reads full. send_data() then returns -EBUSY, and the
mailbox core keeps the message queued without starting the TX poll:
nothing is sent, mbox_send_message() still returns success, and the
client times out waiting for an answer to a command the EB never got.
The queued pointer is sent with the next message, by which time it
points at a dead stack frame.

On the MT6858 this left the GPU unable to power on or off after a few
minutes of runtime PM ("No answer to GPUFreq IPI command 8", then
"Failed to boot MCU").

The IRQ stays masked until the thread returns, so the channel can be
marked empty as soon as the message has been read and acknowledged.
---
 drivers/mailbox/mtk-gpueb-mailbox.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mailbox/mtk-gpueb-mailbox.c b/drivers/mailbox/mtk-gpueb-mailbox.c
index ad5230fd2..9bb4f4aad 100644
--- a/drivers/mailbox/mtk-gpueb-mailbox.c
+++ b/drivers/mailbox/mtk-gpueb-mailbox.c
@@ -116,8 +116,9 @@ static irqreturn_t mtk_gpueb_mbox_thread(int irq, void *data)
 
 		mtk_gpueb_mbox_read_rx(buf, ch);
 		writel(BIT(ch->num), ch->ebm->mbox_ctl + GPUEB_MBOX_CTL_IRQ_CLR);
-		mbox_chan_received_data(&ch->ebm->mbox.chans[ch->num], buf);
+		/* The client may send its next message as soon as it has this one */
 		atomic_set(&ch->rx_status, 0);
+		mbox_chan_received_data(&ch->ebm->mbox.chans[ch->num], buf);
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
 
-- 
